<main class="wide app-pulse">

<style>
  @keyframes pulse-beat {
    0%   { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(43, 212, 168, .5); }
    70%  { box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px rgba(43, 212, 168, 0); }
    100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(43, 212, 168, 0); }
  }
  @keyframes pulse-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .app-pulse .pulse-live .dot,
    .app-pulse .pulse-state .spin { animation: none; }
  }
</style>

<header class="pulse-head">
  <h1 class="pulse-title"><span class="pulse-mark">◐</span><span><span class="pulse-name">Pulse</span><span class="pulse-sub">infrastructure status</span></span></h1>
  <span class="pulse-live"><span class="dot"></span>live · all regions</span>
</header>

A status board for eight services across four regions. The grid below is a keyed `@loop` over fetched JSON, the rollups are `:computed`, and the loading / error / empty states are the four branches of one `:fetch` — no JavaScript written by hand.

:fetch board from "/__wd/data/metrics.json"

## Overview

:computed totalServices = board.services.length

<div class="pulse-stats">

::: stat .is-ok
**Services tracked**

::: div .stat-value
{ totalServices }
:::

Across iad · sfo · fra · global
:::

::: stat .is-ok
**Build-time render**

::: div .stat-value
0 KB
:::

Framework JS until this page fetched
:::

::: stat .is-warn
**Live snapshot**

::: div .stat-value
06:05
:::

Sampled this morning, UTC
:::

::: stat
**Data source**

::: div .stat-value
JSON
:::

One `:fetch`, four lifecycle states
:::

</div>

<div class="pulse-bar">

:button "↻ Refresh feed" -> board refetch
:button "Simulate refresh" -> board refetch

</div>

The two buttons above both call `board refetch` — Darkmown re-runs the request, flips `board_loading` on, then swaps the grid back in. Watch the live dot and the network tab.

## Feed status

A single `:fetch` exposes four reactive flags — `board_loading`, `board_error`, `board_empty`, and the data itself. Each branch below renders for exactly one of them:

:if board_loading
::: div .pulse-state .is-loading
<span class="spin"></span> Polling metrics endpoint…
:::
:else if board_error
::: div .pulse-state .is-error
✕ Feed unreachable — `board_error` holds: { board_error }
:::
:else
::: div .pulse-state
✓ Feed healthy — { totalServices } services reporting. Last sample loaded from `/__wd/data/metrics.json`.
:::
:endif

To prove the **error** branch, here is the same primitive pointed at a URL that 404s — it never resolves to data, so its error flag stays lit:

:fetch missing from "/__wd/data/does-not-exist.json"

:if missing_error
::: div .pulse-state .is-error
✕ `does-not-exist.json` → { missing_error }
:::
:else if missing_loading
::: div .pulse-state .is-loading
<span class="spin"></span> Trying the missing endpoint…
:::
:else
::: div .pulse-state
Waiting…
:::
:endif

And the **empty** branch — a fetch against a file that is literally `[]`. The loop's `@empty` clause renders the moment the result has zero rows:

:fetch incidents from "/__wd/data/empty.json"

@loop incidents into incident
::: div .pulse-state .is-error
{ incident.title }
:::
@empty
::: div .pulse-state .is-empty
○ No active incidents — `@empty` renders instead of any rows. All clear.
:::
@endloop

## Services

<div class="pulse-legend">
  <span class="lg-ok">operational</span>
  <span class="lg-warn">degraded</span>
  <span class="lg-down">outage</span>
</div>

Each card is one row of `@loop board.services into s sort by s.latency desc`. The left rail color, the pill, and the metric tint all come from a reactive `.class when` keyed off `s.status` — no per-row JavaScript. Sorted slowest-first so the trouble floats to the top.

:state showAll = true

:button "Show all" -> showAll = true
:button "Only problems" -> showAll = false

:if showAll

<div class="pulse-grid">

@loop board.services into s sort by s.latency desc
::: card .svc .svc-ok when s.status == "ok" .svc-warn when s.status == "warn" .svc-down when s.status == "down"
::: div .svc-top
::: div .svc-name
**{ s.name }**
::: div .svc-region
{ s.region }
:::
:::
::: pill
{ s.status }
:::
:::
::: div .svc-metrics
::: div .svc-metric
::: div .m-val .is-latency
{ s.latency }ms
:::
::: div .m-key
latency
:::
:::
::: div .svc-metric
::: div .m-val
{ s.uptime }%
:::
::: div .m-key
uptime
:::
:::
:::
::: div .svc-spark
:::
:::
@empty
::: div .pulse-state .is-empty
○ No services in the feed.
:::
@endloop

</div>

:else

Filtered to `where s.status != "ok"` — the same loop, one extra clause. Healthy services drop out live; if everything recovers, `@empty` takes over.

<div class="pulse-grid">

@loop board.services into s where s.status != "ok" sort by s.latency desc
::: card .svc .svc-warn when s.status == "warn" .svc-down when s.status == "down"
::: div .svc-top
::: div .svc-name
**{ s.name }**
::: div .svc-region
{ s.region }
:::
:::
::: pill
{ s.status }
:::
:::
::: div .svc-metrics
::: div .svc-metric
::: div .m-val .is-latency
{ s.latency }ms
:::
::: div .m-key
latency
:::
:::
::: div .svc-metric
::: div .m-val
{ s.uptime }%
:::
::: div .m-key
uptime
:::
:::
:::
::: div .svc-spark
:::
:::
@empty
::: div .pulse-state .is-empty
✓ Nothing degraded — every service is operational.
:::
@endloop

</div>

:endif

The toggle flips a `:state showAll`; the `:if` chooses between the full grid and a `where s.status != "ok"` variant. Both are the same `@loop`, reconciled by key — the runtime patches rows in place instead of re-rendering the list.

<details class="source-reveal"><summary>View source — it's Markdown</summary>

```wd
:fetch board from "/__wd/data/metrics.json"

:computed totalServices = board.services.length

:if board_loading
Polling metrics endpoint…
:else if board_error
Feed unreachable — { board_error }
:else
Feed healthy — { totalServices } services reporting.
:endif

:button "↻ Refresh feed" -> board refetch

@loop board.services into s sort by s.latency desc
::: card .svc .svc-ok when s.status == "ok" .svc-warn when s.status == "warn" .svc-down when s.status == "down"
**{ s.name }** — { s.region }
::: span .pill
{ s.status }
:::
{ s.latency }ms latency · { s.uptime }% uptime
:::
@empty
No services in the feed.
@endloop
```

</details>

